-- title:
--   Two mod-p readings of the j-finite chart ring of X_H(M)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, and let $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ contain every unit whose image in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is $1$. Assume $j$, in its $q$-expansion form `jqModC ℚ` $= q^{-1}\cdot(\text{the integral power series } E_4^3\eta^{-24}\text{-numerator }$`jNum`$)$, lies in the subfield $F(\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}))$ of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by ratios of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms. Write $\mathcal{O}_\Gamma$ for `chartAlgFin`, the subalgebra of elements of $F(\Gamma)$ integral over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}[j]$, where $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ is the subring of rationals with denominator coprime to $p$. Given a $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-algebra map $\iota_0 : \mathcal{O}_{\Gamma_N} \to \mathcal{O}_{\Gamma_M}$ for the groups `ΓN p M H hpM`, `ΓM M H` which preserves $q$-expansions, and a $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-algebra automorphism $\theta$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\Gamma_M}$ whose $q$-expansion on the image of $\iota_0$ is the substitution $q \mapsto q^p$, there exist ring homomorphisms $\theta_0, \theta_1 : \mathcal{O}_{\Gamma_M} \to \mathbb{F}_p((q))$ such that: $\theta_1 = \theta_0 \circ \theta$; whenever $y \in \mathbb{Z}_{(p)}((q))$ has image the $q$-expansion of $c$, $\theta_0(c)$ is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo $p$; $\ker\theta_0 \ne \ker\theta_1$; the minimal primes of the ideal generated by $p$ in $\mathcal{O}_{\Gamma_M}$ are exactly $\ker\theta_0$ and $\ker\theta_1$; and, for $b$ in $\mathcal{O}_{\Gamma_N}$, $\theta_0(\theta(\iota_0 b)) = \theta_0(\iota_0 b)^p$ and also $\theta_0(\theta(\iota_0 b))$ is the substitution $q \mapsto q^p$ applied to $\theta_0(\iota_0 b)$.
--
--   This is the coefficient-field-free form of the two mod-$p$ Gauss readings of the $j$-finite chart ring of the integral model of $X_H(M)$ at a prime exactly dividing the level: the two branches of the fibre at $p$ (Deligne–Rapoport, Katz–Mazur), indexed by the two minimal primes of $(p)$, realised concretely as $\mathbb{F}_p((q))$-valued $q$-expansion homomorphisms exchanged by $\theta$, which acts as Frobenius on functions pulled back from level $M/p$. It feeds the count of minimal primes after base change to an arbitrary algebraically closed field, the construction of retractions compatible with the embedding, and the unramifiedness statements for the quotients used in the level-lowering step.
